module gunbc.constructor_binding_channel

import std.types { List, String, Bool, Int }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }

// THE FOURTH BINDING CHANNEL, ESTABLISHED BY EXECUTION RATHER THAN BY READING THE FOLD.
//
// SUBJECT. Three name-binding channels were already on the record: import resolution, the
// flattened corpus pool (`v1.compiler.infer_env` `global_bare_fallback_invariant`), and the v1
// interpreter's flat bare-name map. This carrier asks whether CONSTRUCTOR (coproduct arm)
// references are a FOURTH -- a channel that binds a name by a mechanism none of those three
// describes -- and answers ESTABLISHED, on a discriminating pair measured at 9917d4a9b3.
//
// WHY THE QUESTION IS NOT ANSWERED BY THE RULING. `v1.compiler.infer` `constructor_binding_authority`
// rules a module's constructor namespace FLAT: its own coproduct declarations plus its DIRECT
// imports, never transitive ancestry. `build_local_variants` and `build_imported_variants` implement
// exactly that, with a checked insert that refuses a same-name/different-owner collision as
// VariantCollision. But `merge_global_bare_variant_locals` then merges a WHOLE-CLOSURE base --
// `build_global_bare_variant_locals`, computed from the corpus census -- underneath that fold, with
// no import and no containment test, and the result is folded into the module's ordinary `locals`
// (`build_module_context`). So the ruling describes two of the three sources the map ends up with.
//
// WHAT THE CONSTRUCTOR HALF OF THIS CARRIER DOES AND DOES NOT SAY ABOUT EMISSION. The channel
// finding below is about BINDING and is independent of what the emitter later harvests. Where this
// carrier does reach emission -- the second next rung -- the claim is deliberately narrow: the
// invisible form is the BARE NULLARY variant value reference, not constructors generally. The broad
// form is refutable by one grep at collect_value_ref_names, which harvests the call and record-literal
// forms, and a reviewer who lands on that arm would dismiss this finding along with the false half.
//
// WHY IT IS A CHANNEL AND NOT THE POOL WEARING A HAT. The pool channel and this one were run
// against ONE fixture shape differing only in what the unimported name is used AS. A type
// reference is admitted with a located `unlisted import use` ADVISORY -- the observation that feeds
// reference-derived Rust use-line emission. The constructor reference in the same position is
// admitted with NO diagnostic of any kind. Same absent import, same absent containment relation,
// two different observabilities: the advisory channel does not cover constructors.
//
// WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, AS CORRECTED. The original sentence here read: "This is not a
// silent-arbitrary-pick finding. With two owners of one arm name inside the compiled closure the
// compile REFUSES (case5)." That generalised case5 past its own geometry and is FALSE in three of
// the four geometries measured below. It is corrected in place rather than deleted, because the
// false form is what a reader would otherwise carry away, and because a lane acting on it would
// conclude the channel already fails closed and stop looking.
//
// What case5 actually establishes is narrower: when the referring module reaches BOTH owners
// DIRECTLY, by its own references, the compile refuses. Reach either owner only indirectly -- a
// carrier module in the closure imports it, and nothing else does -- and the wall does not apply,
// because the fold it lives in (insert_variant_owner_checked, over the module's own declarations
// and its DIRECT imports) never sees the pair. So the honest statement of the channel is that it
// refuses on the per-FILE pair and is silent on the per-CLOSURE one, and the defects named as
// next rungs below stand alongside a silent-wrong-bind finding rather than instead of one.
//
// AND THE SITE OF THAT SILENT BIND IS NOT WHERE THIS CARRIER FIRST SAID IT WAS. The first draft
// of these rows attributed case6 and case7 to `build_global_bare_variant_locals` -- Unique enters
// the whole-closure variant base, Ambiguous falls to its `_ => acc`. That is FALSE for a
// standalone competitor and is corrected here rather than quietly amended, because it is the same
// failure this change exists to fix, one layer down: a plausible mechanism story that a repair
// would be aimed at, landing nowhere near the live site (review 61874). That builder inserts ONLY
// when the Unique binding's owner is a Disj carrying a child of the name, so a foreign
// `type Sq { .. }` -- a Conj -- never enters that base under Unique either, and the fold cannot
// distinguish case6 from case7 at all.
//
// THE LIVE SITE IS RECORD-LITERAL INFERENCE, and the deciding value is `type_name_declares_own_type`.
// For `Sq { s: 2 }` inside the subject: `lookup_variant_parent_enum` finds the LOCAL owner `Shape`
// correctly, so the widening the join needs is available. It is then DISCARDED, because
// `lookup_binding_by_name` resolves the bare `Sq` through `global_bare` to the foreign standalone
// declaration, and `binding_declares_name` is simply "the resolved node's authored name equals the
// looked-up name" -- which a `type Sq` satisfies. The `if` takes the declares-own-type arm and
// keeps the foreign Product instead of widening to the parent. case7 is clean for the same reason
// read backwards: a second competitor makes the bare lookup Ambiguous, `type_name_declares_own_type`
// goes false, the else arm looks the parent up by name, and the local `Shape` wins.
//
// THAT ALSO EXPLAINS case9 WITHOUT A SECOND MECHANISM, which is the check that the story is right
// rather than merely different: a foreign COPRODUCT owning an arm spelled `Sq` resolves the bare
// name to the OWNER node, whose authored name is its own (`Boxone`), not `Sq`. So
// `binding_declares_name` is false, the arm cannot trigger the preference, and it equally cannot
// contribute the ambiguity that would repair case6 -- which is precisely what case9 and case10
// measure. One predicate accounts for all five rows.

// WHAT THE REFERRING MODULE USES THE UNIMPORTED NAME AS. The two arms are the discriminator: they
// are the only difference between case1 and case4.
type ReferenceKind
  = ConstructorReference { position: String }
  | TypeReference { position: String }

// WHAT THE COMPILER DID WITH IT, at the grain that distinguishes the channels. BoundSilently is not
// a synonym for BoundWithAdvisory: an advisory is a located observation a downstream pass reads,
// and its absence is the finding.
type ProbeOutcome
  = BoundSilently { emitted: String }
  | BoundWithAdvisory { advisory: String }
  | RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: String, situation: String }

type ChannelProbe {
  case_name: String
  reference_kind: ReferenceKind
  owner_modules_in_source_root: Int
  owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: Int
  outcome: ProbeOutcome
  what_it_establishes: String
}

// THE MEASUREMENT. Five compiles of hand-authored two- and three-module fixtures, run at
// 9917d4a9b3 through `gunbc compile --source-root <case> --entry <case>/user.dag --target dag`
// on a BuildBuddy runner. Every fixture's referring module is `zqxbeta.user` and every owner is
// `zqxalpha.owner` or `zqxgamma.rival`: no import statement anywhere, and no module path is a
// leading-segment prefix of another, so neither the import channel nor a containment-chain walk
// can account for a binding. The fixture sources are recorded verbatim below so the run is
// re-derivable without archaeology.
data constructor_binding_channel_probes: List<ChannelProbe> = [
  {
    case_name: "case1 -- constructor reference, one owner, no import",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "let initializer and two match patterns" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 1,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 1,
    outcome: BoundSilently { emitted: "1 file emitted, 0 diagnostics, exit 0" },
    what_it_establishes: "a coproduct arm binds across modules with no import and no containment relation, and reports nothing at all. GUNBC_BARE_PULL_TRACE names the route: [bare-pull] user.dag -> ZqxProbeRed -> zqxalpha.owner [scoped unique]",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case2 -- constructor reference naming nothing",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "let initializer" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 0,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 0,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "undefined variable 'ZqxProbeMauve'", situation: "accurate -- no declaration of that name exists" },
    what_it_establishes: "the harness has the power to reject. Without this row case1's green is not evidence of anything",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case3 -- two owners in the SOURCE ROOT, one in the closure",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "let initializer and two match patterns" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 2,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 1,
    outcome: BoundSilently { emitted: "1 file emitted, 0 diagnostics, exit 0" },
    what_it_establishes: "the ambiguity domain is the compiled CLOSURE, not the source root. A second module claiming the same arm name is present and indexed in the name census, and the binding is made anyway. THE CONSEQUENCE IS THE PART LEAST LIKELY TO BE RE-DERIVED: adding an unrelated module to a closure can change which declaration an existing reference denotes, with nothing reported -- the same class as the interpreter's walk-order bare-name map, reached from a different stage",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case4 -- TYPE reference in the identical no-import position (the control)",
    reference_kind: TypeReference { position: "parameter type annotation" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 1,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 1,
    outcome: BoundWithAdvisory { advisory: "advisory[user.dag:5:26]: unlisted import use 'ZqxProbeColor' (referenced but not in any import's name list)" },
    what_it_establishes: "THE DISCRIMINATOR. Identical fixture shape, identical absent import; the type channel is observable and the constructor channel is not",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case5 -- two owners INSIDE the compiled closure",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "let initializer, both owners reached by separate references" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 2,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 2,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "undefined variable 'ZqxProbeRed'", situation: "MISLEADING -- the name is declared twice, not zero times. The channel fails closed, and then describes the closure as if the declaration were absent" },
    what_it_establishes: "the channel does not silently pick a winner under in-closure ambiguity. It refuses -- under a diagnostic that names the wrong situation. READ CASE6 THROUGH CASE10 BEFORE GENERALISING THIS ROW: its geometry has the referring module reaching BOTH owners DIRECTLY, and that is what the wall covers",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case6 -- one foreign STANDALONE type competing with an arm, reached only indirectly",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "the else branch of an if whose join is the declaring module's own coproduct" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 2,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 2,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "if branches resolve to incompatible types: Coproduct(Shape) vs Product(Sq)", situation: "MISLEADING IN A SECOND WAY, distinct from case5's. Nothing is reported as ambiguous or absent; the arm is bound to the FOREIGN declaration and the only observable is a type error at declaring.dag, a file that neither declares nor imports the competitor and is byte-identical to the arm that compiles clean" },
    what_it_establishes: "the per-file wall of case5 does not reach here. No single file imports two owners: the competitor is reached foreign -> carrier -> entry, so insert_variant_owner_checked never sees the pair and the whole-closure base binds it unopposed. This is the silent-arbitrary-pick the original WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED denied",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case7 -- the SAME geometry with a SECOND standalone competitor added",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "identical to case6, byte-identical declaring module" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 3,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 3,
    outcome: BoundSilently { emitted: "11 files emitted, 0 diagnostics, exit 0 -- and the bind is CORRECT" },
    what_it_establishes: "THE NON-MONOTONICITY, IN ISOLATION. Adding a competitor REPAIRS the compile. The mechanism is `type_name_declares_own_type` in record-literal inference, NOT the variant-locals builder this row first named: with one competitor the bare `Sq` resolves through global_bare to the foreign standalone declaration, whose authored name IS `Sq`, so the predicate holds and the foreign Product is kept instead of widening to the local parent the lookup already found; with two, the bare lookup goes Ambiguous, the predicate goes false, and the else arm resolves the parent by name and widens correctly. The consequence is unchanged by the correction: a repair validated on a corpus where most spellings have several answers will look correct and still be wrong, and any severity census that ranks by competitor count has the sign backwards",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case8 -- case6 plus one NON-competing foreign module (the closure-size control)",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "identical to case6" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 3,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 3,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "if branches resolve to incompatible types: Coproduct(Shape) vs Product(Sq)", situation: "same as case6" },
    what_it_establishes: "case7's repair is not an artefact of closure size or module count. This closure is the same size as case7's and stays red; the only variable that moves the verdict is how many declarations answer to the one SPELLING",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9 -- the competitor is a foreign COPRODUCT ARM rather than a standalone type",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "identical to case6" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 2,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 2,
    outcome: BoundSilently { emitted: "9 files emitted, 0 diagnostics, exit 0 -- and the bind is CORRECT" },
    what_it_establishes: "AN ARM IS NOT A COMPETITOR ON THIS CHANNEL. Measured at one and at two such foreign coproducts, both clean. The committed fixture at fixtures/if_join_pool_binding declaring its perturbation as `type PoolSpecimenSquare { s: Int }` -- a standalone product, not an arm -- is therefore load-bearing rather than incidental, and a census that counts arm-shaped answers to a spelling is measuring a population that does not perturb",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case10 -- one standalone competitor AND one coproduct-arm competitor",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "identical to case6" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 3,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 3,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "if branches resolve to incompatible types: Coproduct(Shape) vs Product(Sq)", situation: "same as case6" },
    what_it_establishes: "THE SCOPE OF CASE9 AND CASE10, STATED BEFORE THE FACT SO THE FACT IS NOT OVER-READ. In every one of these five geometries the LOCAL declarer is in the closure throughout, so the closure census for the spelling is never Unique-on-a-FOREIGN-arm. What is measured is that adding an arm owner BESIDE an already-present local declarer changes nothing; what is NOT measured is a closure whose count of arm owners crosses one with no local declarer present, which case3 says is the domain that decides. A reader taking case9 as `arm owners never matter` has taken it past its own geometry, which is the same over-reading this change corrects in case5. Now the fact itself: the two previous rows are one fact, not two. An arm-shaped answer does not perturb AND does not count toward the ambiguity that would have repaired case6 -- had it counted, this closure would have gone clean like case7. So the competitor population is non-monotone in one direction and blind in the other, which is the whole reason these five rows are recorded rather than summarised",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case11 -- the competitor is a foreign COPRODUCT whose OWN NAME is the contested spelling",
    reference_kind: ConstructorReference { position: "identical to case6" },
    owner_modules_in_source_root: 2,
    owner_modules_in_compiled_closure: 2,
    outcome: RefusedWithDiagnostic { diagnostic: "if branches resolve to incompatible types: Coproduct(Shape) vs Coproduct(Sq)", situation: "the same silent wrong bind as case6, and the RENDERED SHAPE IS THE RECEIPT: it says Coproduct(Sq), so the arm bound to the foreign coproduct itself" },
    what_it_establishes: "THE DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION THAT SEPARATES THE TWO MECHANISM STORIES, run because a corrected causal claim asserted from reading is worth less than one that predicted an unmeasured outcome. The refuted story -- the whole-closure variant base -- requires an owner that is a Disj CARRYING A CHILD of the name; this foreign coproduct is a Disj and has NO child spelled Sq, so that story predicts CLEAN. The corrected story turns on binding_declares_name, the resolved node's authored name equalling the looked-up name, which this declaration satisfies, so it predicts PERTURBATION. IT PERTURBS. The arms already recorded separated the two stories only by a structural argument; this row separates them by an outcome neither had been measured against, and the rendered Coproduct(Sq) names the winner directly. It also bounds what case9 says: an arm is not invisible because its OWNER is a coproduct -- a coproduct competes perfectly well when it is the coproduct's own NAME that collides. What is invisible is a name that a declaration does not itself declare",
  },
]

// THE CODE THIS CHANNEL IS MADE OF, cited by symbol so a reader verifies the mechanism rather than
// the narrative. Ordered along the path a constructor name takes.
type ChannelStage {
  site: DeclarationRef
  what_it_contributes: String
  is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: Bool
}

data constructor_binding_channel_stages: List<ChannelStage> = [
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "build_local_variants"),
    what_it_contributes: "the module's own coproduct arms, inserted through insert_variant_owner_checked, which refuses a same-name different-owner pair as VariantCollision",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: true,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "build_imported_variants"),
    what_it_contributes: "the DIRECT imports' contributions, through the same checked insert",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: true,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "merge_global_bare_variant_locals"),
    what_it_contributes: "a whole-closure base merged UNDER the fold above by map_merge, so no collision arm runs over it at all -- the module's own and imported entries simply overlay it",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: false,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "build_global_bare_variant_locals"),
    what_it_contributes: "that base: every corpus-census name whose GlobalBareUniqueBinding resolves to a Disj node owning a child of the same name. Uniqueness across the closure is the only admission test; import and containment are not consulted",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: false,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "build_module_context"),
    what_it_contributes: "folds the result into the module's ordinary locals, so a corpus-derived arm is an ordinary top-priority local binding rather than a fallback consulted last",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: false,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_env", decl_name: "binding_declares_name"),
    what_it_contributes: "THE DECIDING PREDICATE FOR case6 THROUGH case10, and it is one line: the resolved node's authored name equals the looked-up name. A foreign standalone `type Sq` satisfies it; a foreign coproduct owning an ARM spelled Sq does not, because the bare name resolves to the OWNER, whose authored name is its own. That single asymmetry is why a standalone competitor perturbs and an arm does not",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: false,
  },
  {
    site: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_record_lit_structural"),
    what_it_contributes: "where that predicate is CONSUMED and the damage is done: `lookup_variant_parent_enum` has already found the correct LOCAL owner, and the `type_name_declares_own_type` arm then discards it and keeps the foreign declaration instead of widening to the parent. The else arm -- taken when the bare lookup is Ambiguous -- resolves the parent by name and is correct, which is why adding a second competitor REPAIRS the compile",
    is_governed_by_the_flat_ruling: false,
  },
]

// THE FIXTURE SOURCES, recorded rather than left in an untracked directory. Every case's referring
// module is the same shape; only the reference kind and the owner population change. Re-deriving
// the measurement is: write these files under one directory per case, then run the compile named in
// the probe roster's header.
type FixtureModule {
  case_name: String
  file_name: String
  module_source: String
}

data constructor_binding_channel_fixtures: List<FixtureModule> = [
  {
    case_name: "case1, case3, case4, case5",
    file_name: "owner.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxalpha.owner\n\ntype ZqxProbeColor = ZqxProbeRed | ZqxProbeBlue\n",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case3, case5",
    file_name: "rival.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxgamma.rival\n\ntype ZqxRivalColor = ZqxProbeRed | ZqxRivalGreen\n",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case1, case3",
    file_name: "user.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxbeta.user\n\ntype ZqxAnswer = ZqxYes | ZqxNo\n\nfn zqx_probe_pick() -> ZqxAnswer {\n    let probe = ZqxProbeRed\n    match probe {\n        ZqxProbeRed => ZqxYes\n        ZqxProbeBlue => ZqxNo\n    }\n}\n",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case2",
    file_name: "user.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxbeta.user\n\ntype ZqxAnswer = ZqxYes | ZqxNo\n\nfn zqx_probe_pick() -> ZqxAnswer {\n    let probe = ZqxProbeMauve\n    match probe {\n        ZqxProbeMauve => ZqxYes\n    }\n}\n",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case4",
    file_name: "user.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxbeta.user\n\ntype ZqxAnswer = ZqxYes | ZqxNo\n\nfn zqx_probe_type_ref(c: ZqxProbeColor) -> ZqxAnswer {\n    ZqxYes\n}\n",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case5",
    file_name: "user.dag",
    module_source: "module zqxbeta.user\n\ntype ZqxAnswer = ZqxYes | ZqxNo\n\nfn zqx_probe_pick() -> ZqxAnswer {\n    let probe = ZqxProbeRed\n    match probe {\n        ZqxProbeRed => ZqxYes\n        ZqxProbeBlue => ZqxNo\n    }\n}\n\nfn zqx_rival_pick() -> ZqxAnswer {\n    let rival = ZqxRivalGreen\n    match rival {\n        ZqxRivalGreen => ZqxYes\n        ZqxProbeRed => ZqxNo\n    }\n}\n",
  },
]

// THE case6-case10 FIXTURE MODULES ARE COMMITTED FILES, NOT STRINGS, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE
// POINT (review 61858). A `module_source` blob is a SECOND REPRESENTATION of a fixture whose home
// is `fixtures/` -- nothing compiles it, nothing can compile it, and it drifts from the thing it
// transcribes with no mechanism that would notice. The roster above is the old form and is left
// alone rather than churned: its five cases were measured on a different tree by a different
// lane, and rewriting them here would restate a measurement this change did not take. It is the
// form to migrate, not the form to extend.
//
// So the modules rostered below are real files under `fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/`,
// and this roster names them by PATH. Re-deriving case6 through case10 is now a command over
// committed bytes rather than a transcription exercise:
//
//   gunbc compile --source-root fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect \
//                 --entry fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/<entry>.dag
//
// WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT BUY, said plainly so the row is not read as coverage: the fixture
// is committed and compilable, and NOTHING RUNS IT. That is a strictly better state than a string
// blob -- a reader can execute it, and it cannot silently disagree with itself -- but it is not
// an executing consumer, and the rung below stays where it is until one exists.
type FixtureModuleFile {
  case_name: String
  path: String
  role: String
}

data constructor_binding_channel_indirect_fixture_files: List<FixtureModuleFile> = [
  {
    case_name: "case6, case7, case8, case9, case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/declaring.dag",
    role: "THE SUBJECT. Declares both arms of its own coproduct and returns one per if-branch. Byte-identical across every case; that invariance is the instrument",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case6, case7, case8, case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/foreign_one.dag",
    role: "a foreign STANDALONE type spelled the same as the subject's arm, with a DIFFERENT field name so a wrong bind cannot typecheck by coincidence",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case7",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/foreign_two.dag",
    role: "the SECOND standalone competitor, and the only difference between case6 and case7",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case8",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/foreign_three.dag",
    role: "a foreign module that does NOT compete for the spelling -- the control that holds closure size constant against case7",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9, case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/cop_one.dag",
    role: "a foreign COPRODUCT owning an arm of the contested spelling, which is the population case9 shows does not perturb",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/cop_two.dag",
    role: "a second such coproduct, for the two-arm-owner arm of case9",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case6, case7, case8, case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/carrier_one.dag",
    role: "THE CARRIER IS THE GEOMETRY. It imports the foreign owner so the entry reaches it INDIRECTLY, which is why no single file presents two owners to insert_variant_owner_checked and the per-file wall of case5 never applies",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case7",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/carrier_two.dag",
    role: "the same, for the second standalone competitor",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case8",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/carrier_three.dag",
    role: "the same, for the non-competing module",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9, case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/ccar_one.dag",
    role: "the same, for the foreign coproduct",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/ccar_two.dag",
    role: "the same, for the second foreign coproduct",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case6",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_a.dag",
    role: "THE ENTRY IS THE VARIABLE. Subject plus one standalone competitor: REFUSES at the subject, which neither declares nor imports the competitor",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case7",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_b.dag",
    role: "subject plus BOTH standalone competitors: CLEAN, and the bind is correct. The non-monotonicity",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case8",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_d.dag",
    role: "subject, one competitor, one non-competitor: same closure size as case7 and still REFUSES, so the variable is competitor count on the spelling and not closure size",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_e.dag",
    role: "subject plus ONE foreign arm owner: CLEAN",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case9",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_f.dag",
    role: "subject plus TWO foreign arm owners: CLEAN. An arm is not a competitor",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case11",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/named_sq.dag",
    role: "a foreign COPRODUCT whose OWN NAME is the contested spelling and whose arms are unrelated -- a Disj with no child of that name, which is what makes it discriminating",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case11",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/ncar_one.dag",
    role: "its carrier, so the reach stays indirect",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case11",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_h.dag",
    role: "REFUSES with Coproduct(Shape) vs Coproduct(Sq) -- the refuted mechanism story predicted CLEAN here and the corrected one predicted this",
  },
  {
    case_name: "case10",
    path: "fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/entry_g.dag",
    role: "one standalone competitor AND one arm competitor: REFUSES, so an arm does not even count toward the ambiguity that would have repaired case6",
  },
]

// WHAT THIS CARRIER DOES NOT DO, stated so a reader does not take it for coverage. Nothing here
// executes on any run: the subject is a MULTI-MODULE closure, and nothing in this repository
// builds these cases into a witness. The rung this class sits at is MITIGATABLE -- both
// measurements were taken once and are re-measured by nothing.
//
// THE TRIGGER THIS PARAGRAPH USED TO NAME WAS ALREADY SATISFIED WHEN IT WAS WRITTEN, and that is
// worth more than the correction (review 61858). It said the trigger was "a compile surface that
// admits a closure of several named .dag sources as one subject", on the strength of
// compile_dag_rust_emit_check taking a single source string. But `tools.multi_module_compile_fixture`,
// over the host `compile_dag_multi_module_fixture`, takes exactly that closure of several named
// sources -- it is what gunbc#10740 consumes for the neighbouring class. A trigger naming a
// capability that already exists CANNOT FIRE, so the class never ranks for climbing and the stall
// is untracked while looking tracked, which is precisely what DESIGN 4b(2) forbids. The tell was
// available here without leaving the file: a trigger written as a capability should be checkable
// by one grep for that capability, and nobody ran it.
//
// THE REAL TRIGGER IS ENROLLMENT, not a missing surface: a `test.claim` module that builds the
// committed fixture modules rostered below into that fixture surface, asserts the case6-versus-case7
// flip, and is admitted to `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` -- the roster row
// without which a witness module is discovered and never run. At that point case6 and case7 become
// the enrollable discriminating pair and case8 the control that keeps it honest.
// A CONTROL WHOSE SUBJECT CANNOT CONTAIN THE CHANGE IS NOT A CONTROL, and this is written down
// because the next person will reach for the instrument it names as evidence, exactly as this lane
// did. `claim_executor --required-regen` re-emits the v1 seed and compares bytes, and a
// `first_generation_equal=true` from it is routinely read as "emission did not move". It cannot mean
// that for the v2 corpus. `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `reference_derived_use_lines_note` records that
// import-bearing HostNative modules -- which is what the whole v1 seed is -- receive `[]` from the
// reference-derived use-line walk. So the seed is insulated from that walk by construction, and a
// change that alters what the walk synthesizes for v2 namespace modules produces a green regen every
// time. Established while measuring a change that could have moved v2 emission: the regen was green
// and proved nothing about the population at risk.
//
// The general form, stated separately from the specimen because the specimen will be repaired and
// the law will not: an instrument establishes a negative only over subjects that could have carried
// the effect. Naming the instrument is not enough -- its SUBJECT has to be checked against the
// class being denied.
data regen_cannot_see_v2_corpus_emission_change: DeclarationRef = decl_ref(
  module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust",
  decl_name: "reference_derived_use_lines_note",
)

// WHY THE PRIOR TRIGGER COULD NOT FIRE, which is the one thing here that is irreducible rationale
// rather than a typed fact, and so is the one thing left in prose (review 61895). The row below
// used to be a String carrying rung, trigger, two commits and a citation; DESIGN 4c rules that a
// String whose sole purpose is commentary is misplaced data, and rung-plus-trigger is exactly the
// shape 4b already types. So the facts moved into carriers and this paragraph keeps only the why.
//
// The trigger this carrier shipped with named "a compile surface that admits a closure of several
// named .dag sources as one subject". That surface already existed when the sentence was written --
// `tools.multi_module_compile_fixture` over the host `compile_dag_multi_module_fixture` -- so the
// trigger could never fire, the class could never rank for climbing, and the stall was untracked
// while looking tracked. The tell was one grep for the capability, and nobody ran it. A trigger
// written as a capability should be checkable that way; if it is not, it is a wish.
type MeasurementEpisode {
  cases: String
  commit: String
  where_run: String
  command: String
  enrolled: Bool
  re_measured: Bool
}

data constructor_binding_channel_measurements: List<MeasurementEpisode> = [
  {
    cases: "case1 through case5",
    commit: "9917d4a9b3",
    where_run: "a BuildBuddy runner",
    command: "gunbc compile --source-root <case> --entry <case>/user.dag --target dag",
    enrolled: false,
    re_measured: false,
  },
  {
    cases: "case6 through case11",
    commit: "413be13f38a",
    where_run: "a session worktree, on a gunbc built from that tree",
    command: "gunbc compile --source-root fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect --entry fixtures/constructor_binding_channel_indirect/uab/<entry>.dag",
    enrolled: false,
    re_measured: false,
  },
]

// THE TWO EPISODES ARE SEPARATE ROWS RATHER THAN ONE SENTENCE because they were taken on different
// trees by different lanes, and a single covering claim misdates one of them. case7 is the row that
// materially changed what this carrier claims, so a re-derivation should start there.
type EvidenceStanding {
  rung: String
  ceiling: String
  next_rung_trigger: String
  why_the_rung_is_not_higher: String
}

data constructor_binding_channel_evidence_standing: EvidenceStanding = {
  rung: "mitigatable",
  ceiling: "mechanically preventable",
  next_rung_trigger: "a test.claim module that builds the rostered fixture modules through tools.multi_module_compile_fixture, asserts the case6-versus-case7 flip, and is admitted to v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes -- the roster row without which a witness module is discovered and never run",
  why_the_rung_is_not_higher: "unbuilt work, NOT an absent capability. The fixture surface exists and the fixture modules are committed; nothing runs them. The new geometries widen what a single unenrolled measurement covers, they do not climb the rung",
}

// THE TWO REPAIRS THIS ESTABLISHES AND DELIBERATELY DOES NOT MAKE. Both sit in v1's infer stage,
// which DESIGN names as load-bearing, and both are the namespace lane's to sequence: they change
// what an occurrence denotes or what refuses, which is precisely the class the wave-admission wall
// governs.
type NextRung {
  what: String
  evidence_row: String
  why_not_here: String
}

data constructor_binding_channel_next_rungs: List<NextRung> = [
  {
    what: "the in-closure ambiguity refusal must name ambiguity, not absence -- two declarations rendered as 'undefined variable' is the state-space conflation DESIGN's failure-mode roster names, with opposite remedies on either side of it",
    evidence_row: "case5",
    why_not_here: "it is a diagnostic-vocabulary change in v1.compiler.infer, and the refusal it replaces is the wall this carrier just established; changing it under a brief to MEASURE it would leave the measurement describing a tree that no longer exists",
  },
  {
    what: "LANDED as gunbc#9423, recorded here rather than deleted because the row's reasoning is what the repair had to satisfy: an unlisted-use observation for BARE NULLARY variant value references, parallel to the type channel's 'unlisted import use' -- but on ITS OWN diagnostic constructor, UnlistedVariantValueUse, never by reusing UnlistedImportUse. Reusing it was tried and withdrawn: v1.compiler.emit_rust group_unlisted_type_names folds typed.diagnostics selecting UnlistedImportUse by constructor alone, and typed.diagnostics carries infer_diags, so the observation would have fed reference_derived_use_lines and CHANGED WHAT PRODUCTION SYNTHESIZES -- which a standing hold forbids until the pre-cut population is counted. A distinct constructor makes byte-identical emission a property of the shape rather than a diff someone re-runs. THE SCOPE IS NARROW ON PURPOSE AND THE BROAD FORM IS FALSE: v1.compiler.emit_rust collect_value_ref_names has four arms, and only ExprVar carrying a VariantValueBinding falls to its `_ => []`. ExprCall harvests unconditionally by authored name and ExprRecordLit harvests through record_lit_ref_names, so a payload-carrying constructor written Foo { .. } or Foo(x) IS already visible to the reference-derived use-line producer, and pattern positions are handled upstream with their own ambiguity refusal. What is invisible is the bare nullary arm -- Absent, Empty, NoConnective, the unit arm of nearly every coproduct in this corpus. Read at 9917d4a9b3 in this tree, after a manager relay claiming the broader scope was corrected",
    evidence_row: "case4 against case1, plus the four arms of collect_value_ref_names read directly",
    why_not_here: "a repair belongs in its own change rather than smuggled into the measurement that motivates it. The narrowing does not soften the consequence: an incomplete census is incomplete whatever the size of the hole, so while one constructor form contributes no observation, a complete content-addressed census of the use-line repair population cannot be built on current instrumentation",
  },
]
